WEBVTT

00:00:08.042 --> 00:00:10.458
Merry Christmas!

00:00:10.458 --> 00:00:13.125
Merry Christmas!

00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:15.125
What a marvelous Christmas Eve!

00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:18.250
Yes, February means Christmas, all right!

00:00:20.042 --> 00:00:22.042
Happy New Year!

00:00:22.042 --> 00:00:23.667
"New Year"
Happy New Year!

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.333
A new year is upon us!

00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:26.625
Tackle your studies and your assassination with new emotion!

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:30.042
"Best Wishes for the New Year"
Tackle your studies and your assassination with new emotion!

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:30.875
"Best Wishes for the New Year"
Now, then...

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:31.667
Now, then...

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:33.625
Time to laze the day away.

00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:35.792
Where's he going with all this?

00:00:35.792 --> 00:00:39.792
So you're trying to take all the fun
year-end events you missed out on

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:42.583
and cram them into February?

00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:44.000
Ah! Exactly right!

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.667
Our only winter break,
and not a single one of you came to visit!

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:51.542
And you were so earnestly worried
and trying so hard on my behalf

00:00:51.542 --> 00:00:54.583
that it didn't feel right
for me to invite you over...

00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:58.333
Dumb thing to fret about
when we were all so bummed out.

00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:00.958
With all that behind you,
now's the perfect time!

00:01:00.958 --> 00:01:04.583
We'll take back the winter break
we lost--all at once!

00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:08.792
Koro Sensei's living life
as frantically as ever.

00:01:08.792 --> 00:01:14.042
But it's already February.
Future-facing February.

00:01:14.042 --> 00:01:18.750
We've got to figure out where
we're going before we say goodbye.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.000
There were 32 days left
before graduation day--

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.917
and before Koro Sensei's dead-line.

00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:33.792
<i>"Wait, just hang on a sec!"</i>

00:01:33.792 --> 00:01:36.792
<i>I scream, but it gets me nowhere</i>

00:01:36.792 --> 00:01:39.250
<i>I put all my strength into being afraid of</i>

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:42.042
<i>The limits that just kept on closing in</i>

00:01:42.042 --> 00:01:44.583
<i>Reality is merciless</i>

00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:47.292
<i>And time is especially tricky</i>

00:01:47.292 --> 00:01:52.583
<i>It's like someone's snatching away</i>
<i>the blanket I just can't sleep without</i>

00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:58.667
<i>We laughed and fretted</i>

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:03.208
<i>Over silly things, nonsensical things</i>

00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:09.333
<i>Once the final bell rings out</i>

00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:13.917
<i>The fun times will be over, too</i>

00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:15.458
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:15.458 --> 00:02:21.458
<i>365 days' worth of lessons shoved into bags</i>

00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:24.542
<i>Like always, like it's "see you tomorrow"</i>

00:02:24.542 --> 00:02:26.083
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:30.167
<i>365 days' worth of happenings</i>

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:35.208
<i>If you've made me an adult,</i>
<i>don't be showing me tears</i>

00:02:35.208 --> 00:02:36.708
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:38.167
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:40.792
"32 Days Till Koro Sensei's Dead-Line"
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:40.792 --> 00:02:43.292
<i>Even if I grow up some more</i>

00:02:43.292 --> 00:02:46.125
<i>They still won't fade a bit</i>

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.000
"20th Period: Valentine's Day Time"
"by Hinata Okano"

00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:05.208
Future plans, eh...?
What high schools are you guys going to?

00:03:05.208 --> 00:03:08.542
Someplace a little lower-level
to give us breathing room.

00:03:08.542 --> 00:03:11.542
Koro Sensei taught us
the fundamentals through senior year--

00:03:11.542 --> 00:03:14.958
high school can be all about
honing our techniques.

00:03:14.958 --> 00:03:19.000
Must be nice! We're really pushing ourselves.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.708
"If you're going into communications,
you need a solid academic record!"

00:03:22.708 --> 00:03:23.750
Or so I've been told.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.542
You sound nothing like him!

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.792
Where are you headed, Karma?

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:33.125
Ah, I'll stay at Kunugigaoka.

00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:34.042
Huh?!

00:03:34.042 --> 00:03:37.250
You mean you'll take
the entrance exam all over again?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.250
I figured you for something better.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.125
I mean, you could get into
the best high schools around.

00:03:42.125 --> 00:03:45.125
Put yourself in the
main-campus students' shoes.

00:03:45.125 --> 00:03:47.458
The guy they thought
they'd chased away is back--

00:03:47.458 --> 00:03:50.167
and standing head and shoulders above them.

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:53.167
What could be better than
seeing those punks' humiliated mugs

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:55.208
for three whole years?

00:03:55.208 --> 00:03:58.125
Such a winning personality.

00:03:58.125 --> 00:03:59.375
Besides,

00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:03.458
there are better schools
for average academic ability,

00:04:03.458 --> 00:04:06.875
but only Kunugigaoka has
students who'd be fun to take on

00:04:06.875 --> 00:04:09.500
in one-on-one academic showdowns.

00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:14.417
I'll have no problem getting the job I'm after.

00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:18.417
I figure I can take this time
to just enjoy a battle or three.

00:04:18.417 --> 00:04:19.958
That's so you, Karma.

00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:24.042
You've got your dream school, right, Nagisa?

00:04:24.042 --> 00:04:25.750
Uh-huh.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.958
And Kayano,

00:04:26.958 --> 00:04:28.375
Sugino,

00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:30.333
and everyone else...

00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:33.625
It's almost time to say goodbye.

00:04:34.625 --> 00:04:37.458
Each of us, going our own way.

00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:41.875
My top pick is
Keisetsu University's high school.

00:04:41.875 --> 00:04:45.958
It's crazy tough, but the best
shortcut for getting into the college

00:04:45.958 --> 00:04:48.167
Mom wanted to send me to.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:51.375
But after college...

00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:55.792
With these odd talents of mine,
out of step with the times,

00:04:55.792 --> 00:05:00.083
I'm not sure what I <i>can </i>be,
or what I <i>want </i>to be.

00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:03.417
But everyone else is figuring it out...

00:05:03.417 --> 00:05:05.875
Nagisa? Nagisa!

00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:08.500
I said, I finished the workbook!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.042
Sorry, Sakura.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:12.500
What are you zoning out for?

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:16.167
Here you were vowing that
you'd give me the academic chops

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:20.000
to march right back into school this term.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.833
It wasn't a vow, exactly--

00:05:21.833 --> 00:05:24.375
more like "it'd be great if you could."

00:05:24.375 --> 00:05:28.083
Hmm. So you're pondering your future?

00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:30.208
Junior-high kids have it rough.

00:05:30.208 --> 00:05:34.333
I don't even know what I want to be.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.833
What is there?

00:05:36.833 --> 00:05:39.542
I mean, apart from being a teacher?

00:05:39.542 --> 00:05:45.958
Ever since I met you,
that's what you've been to me.

00:05:45.958 --> 00:05:47.375
A... a teacher?

00:05:47.375 --> 00:05:50.125
And if you don't want to be a teacher,

00:05:50.125 --> 00:05:53.625
--It took her saying it for me to realize:
--I could let you be my boyfriend!

00:05:53.625 --> 00:05:58.042
people admire those who change them.

00:05:58.042 --> 00:06:00.458
Like a child whose life is saved by a doctor

00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:03.625
admiring doctors and wanting to be one.

00:06:03.625 --> 00:06:06.458
Like a boy bewitched by beautiful skills

00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:09.583
longing to be an assassin...

00:06:09.583 --> 00:06:14.292
Just like I admired that teacher of ours.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:15.417
"Keisetsu U. High School Exam Admission Ticket"

00:06:15.417 --> 00:06:17.958
"Keisetsu U. High School Exam Admission Ticket"
But...

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.000
Hey, what's that?

00:06:21.625 --> 00:06:23.667
Someone's relatives?

00:06:26.292 --> 00:06:29.792
Go, go, Nagisa!

00:06:29.792 --> 00:06:31.375
Go, go, Nagisa!

00:06:31.375 --> 00:06:36.167
Go, go, Nagisa! Yay!

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:39.708
"Beautiful English Cram School"
Wh-What's with this... indistinct mob of giants?!

00:06:39.708 --> 00:06:43.250
"Beautiful English Cram School"
They're overshadowing our school's famous joint send-off!

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.833
"Beautiful English Cram School"
What the heck are you doing, Koro Sensei?!

00:06:45.833 --> 00:06:47.917
Cheering you on, of course!

00:06:47.917 --> 00:06:51.250
How could I not be there
for my dear student's big moment?

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:53.167
Eeeyikes! Is that the time?!

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:58.750
--Hurry, hurry! Hurry up!
--I've got to pop in on Kimura, Kanzaki, Chiba, Hayami, and Hara

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.917
--Hurry, hurry! Hurry up!
--all within the next four minutes!

00:07:00.917 --> 00:07:02.000
Show them what you've got!

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.000
Up, up, and awaaay!

00:07:06.375 --> 00:07:10.125
I'll never be a teacher like that.

00:07:11.792 --> 00:07:14.583
The last career counseling session
is at the end of February,

00:07:14.583 --> 00:07:16.542
after all our entrance exams.

00:07:16.542 --> 00:07:19.500
I have until then to make up my mind.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.667
For now, I'll focus on the target before me!

00:07:23.958 --> 00:07:28.000
"Assassination Classroom, Final Season"
"by Kaede Kayano"

00:07:32.083 --> 00:07:34.333
Why so antsy, Okajima?

00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:34.917
Oh, uh, nothing.

00:07:34.917 --> 00:07:37.292
"Tentacle"
Oh, uh, nothing.

00:07:37.292 --> 00:07:39.500
Valentine chocolates? For shame.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.792
N-No, it's nothing like that!

00:07:41.792 --> 00:07:43.208
Gross.

00:07:43.208 --> 00:07:48.333
Rude much? <i>You </i>only give out
binge-bought cheapo stuff!

00:07:48.333 --> 00:07:50.750
I-I beg your pardon?!

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.542
What do we have <i>here</i>?

00:07:52.542 --> 00:07:55.333
And who are those for, hmm?

00:07:55.333 --> 00:07:59.083
Wh-What do you mean? It's just a formality!

00:07:59.083 --> 00:08:01.750
Th-They could be for anybody!

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:06.167
Oh? Here I was <i>sure </i>you were
giving them to this guy here.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:13.042
--Forgive me! Please forgive me!
--Hiding her true feelings with those ace acting skills...

00:08:13.042 --> 00:08:17.042
--Forgive me! Please forgive me!
--Not even Koro Sensei has tweaked to Kayano's deal.

00:08:17.042 --> 00:08:18.375
Ever since that kiss,

00:08:18.375 --> 00:08:22.792
she's not hiding her feelings for Nagisa--
she's practically cowering in them.

00:08:22.792 --> 00:08:25.417
If we put these two together...

00:08:25.417 --> 00:08:28.792
...we can tease two birds with one stone.

00:08:28.792 --> 00:08:31.417
We've got us a new toy!

00:08:32.917 --> 00:08:36.042
He doesn't have a great self-image.

00:08:36.042 --> 00:08:39.417
Can't imagine being liked by the opposite sex.

00:08:39.417 --> 00:08:44.333
That's why he's afraid--
he thinks he did something bad to you.

00:08:44.333 --> 00:08:47.750
If you don't set him straight,
he may never understand.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.042
I mean...

00:08:49.042 --> 00:08:52.708
I've <i>acted </i>love tons of times
and studied it and stuff,

00:08:52.708 --> 00:08:56.375
but I have no real-life
experience liking a classmate!

00:08:56.375 --> 00:08:59.208
Like, what expression should I make
when I give him the chocolates?

00:08:59.208 --> 00:09:02.333
Well, let's do some recon.

00:09:02.333 --> 00:09:05.250
Just a little covert training.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.250
"Sugino - Kanzaki"

00:09:07.542 --> 00:09:09.500
Yesss! Yesss!

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.625
--I'm glad you're so happy.
--Yesss... Yesss...

00:09:12.625 --> 00:09:15.458
Receiver Sugino is insanely overjoyed,

00:09:15.458 --> 00:09:18.083
but giver Kanzaki is calm.

00:09:18.083 --> 00:09:19.583
Probably just a formality.

00:09:19.583 --> 00:09:22.250
His "insanely overjoyed"
is insanely frightening.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.208
"Chiba - Hayami"

00:09:27.292 --> 00:09:32.708
Wow. High accuracy,
even when firing chocolate bits.

00:09:32.708 --> 00:09:35.708
Here's the rest, as promised.

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:37.125
Thanks.

00:09:37.125 --> 00:09:40.375
Respect. Let's keep it up.

00:09:40.375 --> 00:09:41.542
Yep.

00:09:41.542 --> 00:09:44.750
Their firing distance
is one of a kind, all right.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.542
I can't imitate that...
and I can't tell if she means it.

00:09:48.542 --> 00:09:50.500
"Terasaka's Gang"

00:09:50.833 --> 00:09:53.458
I put real care into making these.

00:09:53.458 --> 00:09:57.250
"Checklist"
And they come with a love letter. I'll be waiting for your answer.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:00.333
"Checklist"
"Care"? You put a <i>curse </i>into these, you mean!

00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:02.208
Guess she got the drop on me.

00:10:02.208 --> 00:10:04.083
Okuda made me a batch that I'd planned

00:10:04.083 --> 00:10:06.167
"Bonus Case"
to put in Terasaka's shoe cubby.

00:10:06.167 --> 00:10:07.917
"Bonus Case"
Cyanidation complete!

00:10:07.917 --> 00:10:11.083
"Bonus Case"
<i>Some </i>folks secretly think chocolates are for something else!

00:10:11.083 --> 00:10:13.083
"Isogai - Kataoka"

00:10:13.083 --> 00:10:15.542
"Commercial Chocolate" "Super Value Set"
Whoa!

00:10:15.542 --> 00:10:15.833
Whoa!

00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:17.958
All this--for me? Are you sure?

00:10:17.958 --> 00:10:21.000
Share them with your brother and sister.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.083
It's bulk commercial stuff
from an ultra-cheap supermarket.

00:10:24.083 --> 00:10:26.583
Took me four hours by bike there and back.

00:10:26.583 --> 00:10:29.167
Before the entrance exams?
Are you gonna be okay?

00:10:29.167 --> 00:10:33.500
No sweat. Me and my first choice,
we've still got a day before the exams.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:34.458
Huh?

00:10:34.458 --> 00:10:38.625
I'm going to a state school.
The same one as you.

00:10:40.375 --> 00:10:43.667
You are? I hope we both get in.

00:10:43.667 --> 00:10:45.083
Yeah.

00:10:45.833 --> 00:10:47.083
See?

00:10:47.083 --> 00:10:49.958
Everyone has their own whys and hows for this.

00:10:49.958 --> 00:10:54.458
Shouldn't you just say
what you want to say in your own way?

00:10:54.458 --> 00:10:57.458
Yeah. Thanks, you two.

00:10:57.458 --> 00:10:59.583
Now, the problem here...

00:11:01.292 --> 00:11:02.417
--...is how infuriating it is to be watched by that gossipy octopus.

00:11:02.417 --> 00:11:05.792
--A couple, a couple! Let the good times roll!
--...is how infuriating it is to be watched by that gossipy octopus.

00:11:05.792 --> 00:11:07.792
Leave that to me.

00:11:07.792 --> 00:11:10.500
Kayano, did you bring the you-know-what?

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.917
Huh? Oh, uh-huh.

00:11:12.917 --> 00:11:17.000
That ought to lock down Koro Sensei for us.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:21.708
Go throw yourself
into giving away that chocolate.

00:11:21.708 --> 00:11:23.125
Uh-huh...

00:11:43.458 --> 00:11:45.625
Where's my chocolate?!
I must have <i>something</i>!

00:11:45.625 --> 00:11:46.958
Someone musta hid it on the mountain!

00:11:46.958 --> 00:11:50.542
Go look, Nagisa! I refuse
to end this day empty-handed!

00:11:59.667 --> 00:12:01.333
Kayano?

00:12:04.708 --> 00:12:05.750
What's wrong?

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:08.167
You're being so quiet.

00:12:08.167 --> 00:12:11.667
Oh, man--my heart's thumping
so hard I can't think!

00:12:11.667 --> 00:12:15.667
How should I look?
What should I say, when I give him this?

00:12:16.917 --> 00:12:19.000
H-Hey, uh, Nagisa...

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.208
Have you figured out your future plans?

00:12:21.208 --> 00:12:25.125
Well, I kind of have an idea
of what I want to be,

00:12:25.125 --> 00:12:28.333
but right now I'm not sure
at all that I can be it.

00:12:29.667 --> 00:12:31.958
A teacher, probably.

00:12:31.958 --> 00:12:34.708
I've seen him look admiringly at Koro Sensei,

00:12:34.708 --> 00:12:40.833
not as a super-creature
or an assassin, but as a teacher.

00:12:40.833 --> 00:12:45.917
I bet he'll give his answer
at the month-end career counseling.

00:12:45.917 --> 00:12:47.833
Huh?

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:50.667
That's Koro Sensei up in that tree.

00:12:50.667 --> 00:12:53.250
He's engrossed in something or other.

00:12:59.958 --> 00:13:02.333
Out of range...

00:13:02.333 --> 00:13:05.500
Guess he's not about
to make himself a sitting duck.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:08.500
Oh, that's right...

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:14.458
I've come to like that face of Nagisa's,
looking straight ahead.

00:13:14.458 --> 00:13:17.042
The reason I didn't become completely empty

00:13:17.042 --> 00:13:19.458
after losing my family and my revenge

00:13:19.458 --> 00:13:22.292
was because Nagisa killed me.

00:13:23.708 --> 00:13:28.042
Because the honest bloodlust
of this killer I faced

00:13:28.042 --> 00:13:31.458
kindly filled the holes in my heart.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:39.083
So with what face,
what words do I give him this?

00:13:39.083 --> 00:13:40.542
Nagisa?

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:48.000
Thank you for staying
by my side this whole year.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:49.250
Here!

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:50.167
For me?

00:13:50.167 --> 00:13:51.083
Yep!

00:13:51.083 --> 00:13:54.458
--B-But, I mean, <i>I'm </i>the one who should be thanking <i>you</i>.
--Okay, mission accomplished! Well done!

00:13:54.458 --> 00:13:57.750
See you tomorrow!
Hope you get into that school!

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.250
Uh, yeah...

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:03.875
Right now, Nagisa is looking straight ahead.

00:14:03.875 --> 00:14:07.708
I can't be next to him, distracting him.

00:14:07.708 --> 00:14:11.167
But I do want to do something to thank him,

00:14:11.167 --> 00:14:14.167
so I'll use my sharpest blade--my acting--

00:14:14.167 --> 00:14:17.000
to cheer him on with my very best smile.

00:14:20.583 --> 00:14:25.083
To kill yourself for someone else
at the moment of truth...

00:14:25.083 --> 00:14:28.458
That part of her is a lot like Ms. Yukimura.

00:14:28.458 --> 00:14:32.250
Ah, how noble.

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.833
No way can I poach
from someone so admirable.

00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:36.667
Say what?

00:14:36.667 --> 00:14:38.292
Nothing.

00:14:38.292 --> 00:14:40.917
Never mind that--

00:14:40.917 --> 00:14:44.333
<i>What</i>, exactly, has Koro Sensei so enthralled?

00:14:44.333 --> 00:14:48.958
Oh, I got Kayano to leave some chocolates,
a certain photo, and a note

00:14:48.958 --> 00:14:50.125
in an obvious spot...

00:14:50.125 --> 00:14:50.542
"To Koro Sensei" "From my sister"
in an obvious spot...

00:14:50.542 --> 00:14:51.667
"To Koro Sensei" "From my sister"
A photo?

00:14:51.667 --> 00:14:52.875
"To Koro Sensei" "From my sister"
If I'd known it would work so well,

00:14:52.875 --> 00:14:57.042
"To Koro Sensei" "From my sister"
I'd've used it in an assassination.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.667
A top-class dinner on Valentine's Day...

00:15:02.667 --> 00:15:05.917
I should have expected
such thoughtfulness from you.

00:15:05.917 --> 00:15:09.292
They say men give back threefold
on White Day next month.

00:15:09.292 --> 00:15:15.125
I'll accept nothing less than
triple both length <i>and </i>girth,

00:15:15.125 --> 00:15:18.125
Karasuma.

00:15:18.125 --> 00:15:21.417
--I'm out.
--Huh? Hey! Wait! Wait! Stay and eat!

00:15:21.417 --> 00:15:23.458
Regular-sized is just fine!

00:15:23.458 --> 00:15:26.292
I'll even make do with fun-sized!

00:15:26.292 --> 00:15:30.375
Such low-class company
for such a high-class place.

00:15:31.625 --> 00:15:33.333
Here--from Hinano.

00:15:33.333 --> 00:15:38.500
She asked me to give it to you.
You're not at school much lately.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.292
Once I see an opening, he's mine!

00:15:41.292 --> 00:15:43.333
...she said.

00:15:43.333 --> 00:15:47.625
She's reading too much into us.
We're not even dating.

00:15:47.625 --> 00:15:49.292
And the others?

00:15:49.292 --> 00:15:53.292
There were more chocolates than I'd thought,
both obligatory and heartfelt.

00:15:53.292 --> 00:15:56.292
Maybe some of them
thought it might turn out to be

00:15:56.292 --> 00:15:58.500
their last Valentine's Day on Earth.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:02.208
And? What about you?

00:16:02.208 --> 00:16:04.250
How's the assassination going?

00:16:05.542 --> 00:16:09.667
"The probability's down
to one percent! Hooray!"

00:16:09.667 --> 00:16:12.708
Like it'll end there.

00:16:12.708 --> 00:16:18.500
So that's why she found
a private room at a trustworthy spot...

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:22.625
Yes. I was planning to talk to you about it.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:27.042
My main job now is solely
to provide guidance to the E Class,

00:16:27.042 --> 00:16:31.375
so they won't put me fully
in the loop until the eleventh hour.

00:16:31.375 --> 00:16:34.167
But there's no doubt that the powers that be

00:16:34.167 --> 00:16:38.958
are moving forward with
a tremendous assassination project.

00:16:41.625 --> 00:16:44.125
To see it again like this--it's just amazing.

00:16:44.125 --> 00:16:46.583
Can this really kill him?

00:16:46.583 --> 00:16:52.167
With this weapon,
it's not a matter of whether it <i>can</i>.

00:16:52.167 --> 00:16:57.333
What's crucial is just how <i>smooth</i>
and how <i>smart </i>it'll do the job.

00:16:59.208 --> 00:17:03.417
A virtuous mind and
a brutally gorgeous figure...

00:17:05.667 --> 00:17:09.583
Not very impressive, seeing one of our teachers

00:17:09.583 --> 00:17:12.250
laid so low by a single swimsuit snapshot.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:14.792
Mr. Principal, sir! Where'd <i>you </i>come from?!

00:17:14.792 --> 00:17:17.167
There are problems with your work attitude.

00:17:17.167 --> 00:17:19.792
I'll be cutting your salary this month.

00:17:19.792 --> 00:17:21.708
Have mercy!

00:17:21.708 --> 00:17:24.208
Ms. Yukimura... is it?

00:17:24.208 --> 00:17:26.958
Pity we had to lose such talent.

00:17:26.958 --> 00:17:31.250
She had an inexhaustible vitality
and such passion for teaching.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:35.000
Given a few more years, she would have
been an outstanding teacher.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.333
Yes.

00:17:36.333 --> 00:17:41.375
By the way, I hear there's
a chance your life may be saved.

00:17:41.375 --> 00:17:44.333
If so, would you care to follow in her footsteps

00:17:44.333 --> 00:17:47.500
and teach here next year as well?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.667
Your forced expression and that body of yours

00:17:49.667 --> 00:17:54.292
are well-suited to teaching
at this satellite campus.

00:17:54.292 --> 00:17:58.167
I'm flattered. For you, who judges
a teacher purely on aptitude

00:17:58.167 --> 00:18:01.292
without being led astray
by sentiment or one's past,

00:18:01.292 --> 00:18:05.833
to try persuading me to stay...
It's the best report card I could want.

00:18:05.833 --> 00:18:06.417
"Roll Book"

00:18:06.417 --> 00:18:11.542
"Roll Book"
But I've decided this will be my last year at the blackboard.

00:18:11.542 --> 00:18:12.708
And after that?

00:18:12.708 --> 00:18:18.417
Who knows? Perhaps I'll sail around the world.

00:18:18.417 --> 00:18:23.792
Having you for a rival
made this school truly enjoyable for me.

00:18:23.792 --> 00:18:27.375
I really must thank you again.

00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:29.000
That's too bad...

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.917
You turned me down before I could bribe you.

00:18:32.792 --> 00:18:36.917
Now that I think about it...
I rule this school from the top,

00:18:36.917 --> 00:18:41.125
while you and Ms. Yukimura
support your students from the bottom.

00:18:41.125 --> 00:18:45.500
That might just be my educational ideal.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:47.708
By the way, how's your son?

00:18:47.708 --> 00:18:51.500
Ah, he's putting together
a ruling hierarchy for high school.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:55.375
At this rate, he'll have the whole place
under his thumb within the year.

00:18:56.333 --> 00:18:58.333
Truly a remarkable young man.

00:18:58.333 --> 00:19:00.792
Oh, he's not quite there yet.

00:19:00.792 --> 00:19:03.583
There's no end to the ways
in which he's still lacking.

00:19:04.833 --> 00:19:06.833
You know, Karasuma,

00:19:06.833 --> 00:19:10.667
I think it might not be so bad
if the world were destroyed.

00:19:10.667 --> 00:19:13.542
For the kids, anyway.

00:19:13.542 --> 00:19:16.292
If they can't kill him,
they'll be left with these nagging feelings

00:19:16.292 --> 00:19:18.833
of frustration and loss.

00:19:18.833 --> 00:19:22.458
Worse, if their teacher were killed
in some huge assassination

00:19:22.458 --> 00:19:25.542
that's out of their league
and beyond their control...

00:19:25.542 --> 00:19:29.125
...or if they were made to watch
their mentor's cruel and painful death

00:19:29.125 --> 00:19:33.458
at the hands of some conflicted assassin...

00:19:35.292 --> 00:19:39.292
It's <i>scary</i>: frustration, powerlessness, trauma.

00:19:39.292 --> 00:19:44.208
No matter what happens,
it's bound to warp those kids' futures.

00:19:44.208 --> 00:19:46.375
I don't want to see those blameless brats

00:19:46.375 --> 00:19:50.083
turn into adults with twisted hearts.

00:19:50.958 --> 00:19:52.375
Irina?

00:19:54.167 --> 00:19:57.500
Once this job is over, quit.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:00.167
You're not cut out to be an assassin.

00:20:00.167 --> 00:20:02.000
<i>What</i>?

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.083
Your emotions run too deep.

00:20:04.083 --> 00:20:07.333
They've grown fatally deep this past year.

00:20:07.333 --> 00:20:10.125
If you feel such emotion for your students,

00:20:10.125 --> 00:20:13.000
it'll only make any
future jobs that much harder.

00:20:17.042 --> 00:20:20.292
A square like you can blow it off easily enough,

00:20:20.292 --> 00:20:23.667
this life I've desperately built for myself...

00:20:23.667 --> 00:20:25.250
I've killed a lot, you know.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.667
There's no going back to a place in the sun--

00:20:27.667 --> 00:20:32.125
not with these ten sin-stained years behind me.

00:20:32.125 --> 00:20:36.500
Every experience is a tool to clear your path.

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:41.792
It was none other than
those students who taught me that.

00:20:41.792 --> 00:20:43.250
Whether you worry or not,

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:45.667
no matter what difficulty they may face,

00:20:45.667 --> 00:20:48.167
the experience they've gained
through assassination

00:20:48.167 --> 00:20:51.542
will nourish them
as they find their own answers.

00:20:51.542 --> 00:20:55.333
Irina, come work for us.

00:20:55.333 --> 00:20:59.875
I'm sure your experience will be
put to good use in peacetime, too.

00:20:59.875 --> 00:21:02.375
The Intelligence Department
won't ask about your past.

00:21:02.375 --> 00:21:05.625
There, you can save
more people than you've killed,

00:21:05.625 --> 00:21:09.875
and pray for your victims
at the shrine every morning.

00:21:09.875 --> 00:21:11.292
That's enough.

00:21:12.583 --> 00:21:14.208
Shrine...?

00:21:14.208 --> 00:21:16.875
But I'm Christian.

00:21:16.875 --> 00:21:20.625
And I have no family in Japan...

00:21:20.625 --> 00:21:25.875
Don't you get it? There aren't
any churches near my house.

00:21:29.542 --> 00:21:32.042
<i>Whaaat</i>?!

00:21:32.042 --> 00:21:34.958
Wait, Karasuma--what are you saying?

00:21:34.958 --> 00:21:36.625
Just what I said.

00:21:36.625 --> 00:21:40.000
B-B-But a man and a woman
living under one roof is so...

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:40.833
...<i>immoral</i>!

00:21:40.833 --> 00:21:42.667
Live alone, then.

00:21:42.667 --> 00:21:44.583
No! I'll do it! I'm coming! Wait up! Karasuma!

00:21:44.583 --> 00:21:46.750
<i>The day I met you felt so far away</i>
No! I'll do it! I'm coming! Wait up! Karasuma!

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:56.542
<i>The day I met you felt so far away</i>

00:21:56.542 --> 00:22:07.500
<i>The memories I've arranged</i>
<i>little by little keep me warm</i>

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:19.042
<i>A small room, hearts connecting:</i>
<i>you taught me gently</i>

00:22:19.042 --> 00:22:31.792
<i>Once this season comes for me, I won't be able</i>

00:22:31.792 --> 00:22:37.042
<i>To search out your figure anymore</i>

00:22:37.042 --> 00:22:42.792
<i>I'll never forget</i>

00:22:42.792 --> 00:23:02.016
<i>Until the day I can see you again</i>
